@abstract:
Declared future intent for PanLL — panel framework with TEA architecture,
Stapeln container integration, and TypeLL core assimilation.
@end

@requires:
- section: Core
- section: Integration
- section: Quality
@end

## Core

### tea-framework
- description: Complete TEA (The Elm Architecture) implementation
- status: in-progress
- priority: critical
- evidence: command: find src/core -name '*TEA*' -o -name '*Update*' -o -name '*Msg*' 2>/dev/null | wc -l | grep -v '^0$'

### workspace-layer
- description: Implement workspace layer for multi-panel management
- status: in-progress
- priority: high
- evidence: command: find src/ -name '*Workspace*' 2>/dev/null | wc -l | grep -v '^0$'

### safedom-v2
- description: SafeDOM v2 with full Nickel contract validation
- status: in-progress
- priority: high
- evidence: contractiles/safedom-enforcement.ncl exists

## Integration

### typell-assimilation
- description: Assimilate TypeLL core into PanLL
- status: in-progress
- priority: critical
- notes: TypeLL provides the type system layer for PanLL's lifecycle

### stapeln-containers
- description: Integrate with Stapeln container system
- status: declared
- priority: high

### idaptik-game-panels
- description: Game development panels for IDApTIK integration
- status: declared
- priority: medium
- evidence: command: find src/ -name '*Game*' 2>/dev/null | wc -l | grep -v '^0$'

## Quality

### test-coverage
- description: Unit tests for core panel lifecycle
- status: declared
- priority: medium

### rescript-migration
- description: Ensure all code uses modern ReScript APIs
- status: in-progress
- priority: high
- evidence: command: grep -rn 'Js\.\(Dict\|Array2\)' src/ --include='*.res' | wc -l | grep -q '^0$'
